WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.610
As every beer commercial ever has pointed
out, friends make life better.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.110
And that's even truer when you want to watch
certain movies, because you need someone to

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:14.059
scream with, someone to grab during the scary
parts, and someone to call at all hours when

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:16.390
nightmares wake you up in a cold sweat.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.349
So find a friend and gather your loved ones
close, because here's a look at some movies

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:22.369
you should never watch alone.

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:23.369
The Ring

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:28.199
Despite the decidedly dated piece of technology
at its center, this movie about a haunted

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:33.100
videotape has actually become even more acutely
unsettling since its release more than a decade

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.100
ago.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.539
Back then, you'd have to deliberately put
the tape in your VCR and press play; but since

00:00:37.539 --> 00:00:41.620
the advent of digital media, you could end
up watching the whole accursed horrifying

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.930
thing on the internet before you knew what
hit you.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.969
It's like a rick-roll that ends in fright!

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:51.420
Plus, if you watch The Ring, you have also
by definition seen that video, so…

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.560
"Never gonna give you up, never gonna let
you down."

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.560
"Rahhhh!"

00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.920
The Descent

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.250
Down we go further into the rabbit hole of
blood-chilling terror, with the aptly-titled

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.040
adventure-horror The Descent.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.450
It tells the tale of a few adventurous young
women gearing up for a spelunking trip in

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.130
the Appalachian Mountains of North Carolina.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:17.130
But everything goes sour when they drop into
the cave — with no way out.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:22.010
Bathed in pitch-black darkness and surrounded
by warped humanoid creatures known as "crawlers"

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:26.829
that are hungry for flesh and blood, the women
are forced to fight their way out of the hole.

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:30.890
And just like a cave expedition, watching
the The Descent is something you should never

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.390
do alone.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:33.930
The Woman in Black

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:38.789
Daniel Radcliffe plays a baby-faced barrister
who uncovers a sinister secret in this historical

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:39.789
horror movie.

00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:44.460
The whole thing features a creepy gothic mansion,
an old-school grudge, and a vengeful ghost

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.810
with an uncanny gift for convincing children
to off themselves.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.460
So, y'know, not really something you should
check out by your lonesome.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.520
There's nothing like a good, old-fashioned
haunted house story to give you the heebie-jeebies

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.750
when you watch it by yourself.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.659
But The Woman in Black raises the stakes by
imbuing every creaking door, every warping

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:06.350
floorboard, and every ordinary household object
with a sense of freaky foreboding.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.130
Even if you don't end up spotting the femme
fatale from the title in her Victorian veil

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:14.770
lurking in a corner, the shadowy walk through
your dark house after watching it is one you

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.160
won't want to make solo.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.370
The Babadook

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:23.290
Written and directed by Aussie triple-threat
Jennifer Kent in her directorial debut, The

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.310
Babadook centers around a mother and her son
stalked by the creepy thing in the movie's

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:32.640
title: a pop-up book monster named Mister
Babadook who threatens multiple slayings if

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.640
anyone denies his existence.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:39.610
"If you're a really clever one and you know
what it is to see, then you can make friends

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:46.470
with a special one, a friend of you and me."

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.060
Following a series of febrile seizures, violent
hallucinations, insomnia-induced blackouts,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.910
and acts of physical aggression, all caused
by the Babadook, Amelia and Sam try valiantly

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.180
to vanquish the beast once and for all.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:05.370
One of the scariest films in recent memory,
The Babadook isn't one to catch alone.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.370
Don't Breathe

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.160
An opportunistic break-in goes terribly wrong
in this film by Fede Alvarez, as a trio of

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.760
small-time teen crooks try to burgle a blind
man who turns out not to be quite as easy

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.510
a target as he originally appeared.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:22.510
The tables turn almost instantly, leaving
the would-be thieves trapped in the dark,

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.090
unfamiliar house where a misstep or cough
could bring their final breath.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:31.760
And Alvarez keeps the tension at an unceasing
fever pitch for the full duration of the movie.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:32.990
Poltergeist

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:37.160
More than three decades after its original
release, Poltergeist is still a who's who

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.810
of terrifying tropes: ghosts reaching out
through the scrambled signals on your TV,

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.790
man-eating trees lurking outside your window,
evil clowns hiding under your bed, and a portal

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.640
to another dimension casually stuffed into
the closet.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:54.070
And no matter how long it's been since you
first saw it, Poltergeist still makes even

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:58.590
the most cookie-cutter suburban tract house
feel like it might be full of otherworldly

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.590
threats.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.980
Without a friend by your side, you'll be too
creeped out to continue on.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.220
"They're heeere!"

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.020
It Follows

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:11.790
The acclaimed horror darling It Follows sparked
a new wave of smartly scary flicks — and

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:16.320
understandably so, as it's a film unlike any
other in its genre.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.620
Directed by David Robert Mitchell, this movie
takes the teen slasher genre and completely

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:26.009
inverts it, replacing gore with an overwhelming,
constant sense of dread and impending doom,

00:04:26.009 --> 00:04:30.370
while slyly commenting on the whole "sex will
get you slayed" message in so many traditional

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.710
teen psycho thrillers.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.900
It Follows strings you along, leaving you
sweaty and skeptical but wholly satisfied,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.520
and will follow you long after its final scene.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.580
Antichrist

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:46.419
Charlotte Gainsbourg and Willem Dafoe star
in this experimental horror flick, which divided

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:52.169
both fans and critics thanks to its twisted
narrative, obscure plot, and viscerally disturbing

00:04:52.169 --> 00:04:53.800
sexual content.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:57.710
Centered on a couple grieving the loss of
their son, the movie starts out with a graphic

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:03.120
sex scene and delves into some seriously dark
places as it explores themes of motherhood,

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.569
grief, misogyny, and sexual violence.

00:05:05.569 --> 00:05:10.569
Not for everyone — or maybe anyone — and
certainly not to be watched alone.

00:05:10.569 --> 00:05:11.569
Deliverance

00:05:11.569 --> 00:05:15.810
A bromantic river-rafting trip turns into
an all-out, life-ruining nightmare in this

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:21.120
classic from 1972, starring Jon Voight and
Burt Reynolds back in their heyday as chiseled

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.280
leading men.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:26.199
Deliverance was a multiple Oscar nominee the
year it was released, which makes it a damn

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:28.310
fine movie by all accounts.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:32.700
But thanks to That Scene — film buffs...you
know the one — it makes for damn uncomfortable

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.700
viewing.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:38.060
Like a trip down the Cahulawassee River, the
narrative journey of Deliverance is one better

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.699
taken with a few close friends.

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:42.409
The Human Centipede

00:05:42.409 --> 00:05:46.680
There may never be another body horror film
as thoroughly, utterly repulsive as The Human

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:52.139
Centipede…except maybe the Human Centipede
sequels, which are just like The Human Centipede,

00:05:52.139 --> 00:05:53.410
but somehow grosser.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:58.270
In this first entry in the series, a demented
scientist kidnaps three people and surgically

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:03.050
attaches them, mouth-to-butt, to create the
"human centipede" from the title — a procedure

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:07.569
touted in the movie's promotional materials
as "one hundred percent medically accurate."

00:06:07.569 --> 00:06:12.330
Despite a broad consensus that The Human Centipede
is profoundly disgusting and lacking in all

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.759
respects except a unique premise, it still
rated decently with critics.

00:06:16.759 --> 00:06:21.289
But much like its central, monstrous surgical
creation, this movie just doesn't work as

00:06:21.289 --> 00:06:23.139
a solo undertaking.

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:24.580
Lake Mungo

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:29.460
This underrated Aussie horror flick is a suspenseful
slow burn from start to finish, as it tells

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:33.810
the story of a family consumed by grief in
the wake of their teenage daughter's accident.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:38.550
It's shot documentary-style and with lots
of creepy tension stemming from barely-glimpsed

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.999
threats and unseen things that go bump in
the night.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:45.469
Lake Mungo spends nearly every one of its
89 minutes building to an incredibly freaky

00:06:45.469 --> 00:06:50.360
climax that'll scare you while
also leaving you with many, many more questions

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.889
than answers.

00:06:51.889 --> 00:06:53.340
Hard Candy

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:57.699
Before she earned raves for playing Juno MacGuff
or walked through walls as Kitty Pryde in

00:06:57.699 --> 00:07:01.580
the X-Men, Ellen Page cut her teeth on a very
different kind of role.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:06.850
Back in 2006, Page played the sadistic, iron-hearted
Hayley Stark in Hard Candy.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:10.809
A 14-year-old who has "victim" written all
over her at the start of the film, Hayley

00:07:10.809 --> 00:07:15.940
quickly turns the tables on Jeff, the 32-year-old
photographer and probable predator she met

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.020
on the internet.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:21.580
After inviting herself to his home, she drugs
him and tortures him in a series of brutal

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.620
scenes that seem to go on forever.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:28.550
Between its suspense and dark subject
matter, Hard Candy isn't a comfortable viewing

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.599
experience, but it's ever so slightly more
bearable if you have a companion to share

00:07:32.599 --> 00:07:34.229
the bad vibes.

00:07:34.229 --> 00:07:35.340
Unfriended

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:40.129
If ever there was a movie best watched with
half a dozen of your closest pals, it's Unfriended.

00:07:40.129 --> 00:07:44.730
Six teenagers on a group chat find themselves
being picked off one by one by an unseen,

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:48.960
Skype-based entity that might or might not
be the ghost of their dead friend.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.210
Unfriended is an original horror story for
the social media age, and it's definitely

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.150
meant to be a group experience.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.440
Feeling extra bold?

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:00.409
Make it a virtual get-together and watch it
with your besties on a Google hangout… and

00:08:00.409 --> 00:08:05.449
hope that nobody experiences any, ahem, technical
difficulties.

00:08:05.449 --> 00:08:06.509
Green Room

00:08:06.509 --> 00:08:10.360
If you thought the other movies on this list
were intense, you haven't seen anything like

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.360
Green Room.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:16.009
An all-out raucous horror picture framed around
a dimly lit hardcore punk show, this film

00:08:16.009 --> 00:08:20.830
skirts the edges of torture porn but spins
toward absurdity with elements reminiscent

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:25.520
of Scott Pilgrim vs. The World, zooming in
on a keen portrayal of what the punk subculture

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.520
is all about.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:31.039
The band at the center of the story is The
Ain't Rights, featuring the late Anton Yelchin

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:35.040
as the bassist Pat and Alia Shawkat on guitar
as Sam.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.570
They open their set list with a cover of the
Dead Kennedys' "Nazi Punks F–k Off" and

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.950
later find the body of a girl backstage.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:46.190
Realizing she'd been slayed, the members
of The Ain't Rights attempt to notify authorities

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:50.850
but are themselves attacked by a group of
neo-Nazis led by the chillingly evil Patrick

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:53.120
Stewart of all people.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.820
"I think I'm smarter than you!"

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:01.960
Mama

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.900
What can compare to a mother's love?

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:08.930
Well, that's exactly what the Guillermo del
Toro-produced movie Mama aims to answer.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:12.970
Starring Interstellar's Jessica Chastain as
the hesitant but well-meaning Annabel and

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:17.490
Game of Thrones' Nikolaj Coster-Waldau in
a double role as the financially devastated,

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:22.650
homicidal Jeffrey and his grief-stricken twin
brother Lucas, this supernatural flick delivers

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:26.540
both a myth buried in maternity and a whole
truckload of scares.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.900
From the shadowy figure that lingers over
Lucas' two feral young nieces to the final

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:35.700
reveal that's equally as haunting, this film
is definitely one worth watching… just,

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:36.700
you know.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.200
Not alone.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.760
Ex Machina

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.910
Robots and red lights and rebellion!

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.300
A true triple-threat in the world of sci-fi.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:48.660
You've likely heard of this Alex Garland-helmed
film, or at least seen Oscar Isaac donning

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:51.000
a full beard and tearing up the dance floor.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.710
Don't be fooled by that unexpected moment
of humor, though.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:58.270
Ex Machina weaves sleek sci-fi with scathing
psychological horror, warning of the possible

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:02.620
dangers of sentient artificial intelligence
and what can happen when you give humans more

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.400
power than they deserve.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.900
Garland makes his directorial debut with this
film — which also stars Isaac's Star Wars:

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:14.370
The Force Awakens costar Domhnall Gleeson,
as well as the newest Lara Croft, Alicia Vikander.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:17.870
But you wouldn't know that a movie this good
could be anyone's first.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:22.420
Ex Machina is sinister and spooky speculative
fiction that feels uncomfortably close to

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.420
reality.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:27.510
You'll likely never look at a piece of technology
the same way again after giving it a watch,

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:32.770
so it's best to have someone by your side
to remind you that yes, humans do still exist.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.320
And no, you don't have to fear the toaster.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:37.920
"Ahhhh!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.240
Ahhhhh!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.040
Ugh, get it off!"

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.090
Thanks for watching!

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:45.620
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.010
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

